<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="Create_A_Room_Level">Create A Room Level</span></h4>
<p>As mentioned above a level is the underlying structure to an area.  For our first level we're going to start with a room level.
</p><p><br style="clear: both" />
</p>
<div class="thumb tleft"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:362px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20001.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/e/e9/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_001.png" width="360" height="520" class="thumbimage" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/e/e9/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_001.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/e/e9/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_001.png 2x" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20001.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>Creating a new level; click File, New, Level.</div></div></div>
<p>Click <b>File</b>, then <b>New</b>, then <b>Level</b>.
</p><p><br style="clear: both" />
</p>
<div class="thumb tleft"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:362px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20002.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/2/29/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_002.png" width="360" height="231" class="thumbimage" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/2/29/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_002.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/2/29/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_002.png 2x" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20002.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>The Level Creation Wizard.</div></div></div>
<p>You'll find yourself in the Level Creation Wizard.  The first screen prompts you to create a terrain, or exterior level, or a room (interior) level.  We're going to walk through the creation of a room level first, so select <b>Room Level</b> and click <b>Next</b>.
</p><p><br style="clear: both" />
</p>
<div class="thumb tleft"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:362px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20003.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/thumb/0/00/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_003.png/360px-Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_003.png" width="360" height="231" class="thumbimage" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/thumb/0/00/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_003.png/540px-Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_003.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/0/00/Talonius_Toolkit_Level_Create_003.png 2x" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20Level%20Create%20003.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>The Level Creation Wizard.</div></div></div>
<p>If we were creating a terrain level there would be a number of options presented to us; the room level creation is much simpler.
</p><p>Click <b>Finish</b> to create the room level.
</p><p><br style="clear: both" />
</p>
<h4><span class="mw-headline" id="A_Tour_of_the_Toolset_Interface">A Tour of the Toolset Interface</span></h4>
<p>The sheer number of icons and options on the toolset can be intimidating.  We're going to highlight the important areas of the interface to help you familiarize yourself with the toolset.
</p><p><br style="clear: both" />
</p>
<div class="thumb tleft"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:362px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20UI%20Walkthrough%20002.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/thumb/1/17/Talonius_Toolkit_UI_Walkthrough_002.png/360px-Talonius_Toolkit_UI_Walkthrough_002.png" width="360" height="467" class="thumbimage" srcset="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/1/17/Talonius_Toolkit_UI_Walkthrough_002.png 1.5x, https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/1/17/Talonius_Toolkit_UI_Walkthrough_002.png 2x" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20UI%20Walkthrough%20002.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>The Palette Window.</div></div></div>
<p>The first section to learn about is the <b>Palette Window</b>.  By default this is located in the upper right hand portion of the toolset screen.  This window is used extensively during the creation of a module.
</p><p>Two things to note:  first, in the upper left corner of the Palette Window are two icons.  The first is a push pin; the second is an X.  
</p>
<div class="thumb tright"><div class="thumbinner" style="width:87px;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20UI%20Walkthrough%20003.png"><img alt="" src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/main/assets/mw/images/1/1e/Talonius_Toolkit_UI_Walkthrough_003.png" width="85" height="312" class="thumbimage" /></a>  <div class="thumbcaption"><div class="magnify"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/File%20-%20Talonius%20Toolkit%20UI%20Walkthrough%20003.png" title="Enlarge"></a></div>The Palette Window and Object Inspector windows collapsed.</div></div></div>
<p>The push pin collapses the window into the sidebar, providing a larger workspace for any remaining open windows.  To reopen the window simply click on the window title in the sidebar.  You can then keep the window open by hitting the push pin icon again.
</p><p>The X closes the window.  If you accidentally close either window they can be opened again from the <b>View</b>, <b>Palette</b> selection and the <b>View</b>, <b>Other Windows</b>, <b>Object Inspector</b> for the Palette Window and Object Inspector windows respectively.
</p><p>Both of these icons can be found with nearly every window within the toolset.
</p><p><b>Palette Window</b>
</p>
